WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.056
I have been building a small project

00:00:02.056 --> 00:00:03.110
called Office Town.

00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:05.802
The reason is pretty simple.

00:00:05.802 --> 00:00:08.272
I often have several AI sessions open.

00:00:08.272 --> 00:00:10.618
I am coding different projects while

00:00:10.618 --> 00:00:12.656
working on Xiaohongshu content.

00:00:12.656 --> 00:00:15.002
One session is changing the training

00:00:15.002 --> 00:00:15.681
platform,

00:00:15.681 --> 00:00:18.274
another is drafting a post or trying out

00:00:18.274 --> 00:00:18.830
titles.

00:00:19.383 --> 00:00:20.474
When I come back,

00:00:20.474 --> 00:00:22.024
I have to check each one.

00:00:22.024 --> 00:00:23.460
Where did we leave off?

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.354
Is anyone waiting for my reply?

00:00:25.354 --> 00:00:27.306
Sometimes I cannot even remember

00:00:27.306 --> 00:00:29.143
everything I asked them to do.

00:00:29.717 --> 00:00:32.167
The records are spread across different

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:32.645
tools.

00:00:32.645 --> 00:00:34.080
Away from my computer,

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.172
picking things up is awkward too.

00:00:36.172 --> 00:00:38.383
I wanted to bring them together and

00:00:38.383 --> 00:00:40.117
check progress on my phone.

00:00:40.683 --> 00:00:42.711
This is the current interface.

00:00:42.711 --> 00:00:45.308
Each employee represents an AI session.

00:00:45.308 --> 00:00:47.525
I can open one to read my earlier

00:00:47.525 --> 00:00:48.159
request,

00:00:48.159 --> 00:00:49.299
see what it did,

00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:51.643
and find anything still unresolved.

00:00:52.217 --> 00:00:53.762
I also added a butler.

00:00:53.762 --> 00:00:56.079
I can ask what needs my attention,

00:00:56.079 --> 00:00:58.397
and it checks the task records for

00:00:58.397 --> 00:01:00.457
anything waiting for my reply.

00:01:03.217 --> 00:01:04.674
For the training platform,

00:01:04.674 --> 00:01:06.757
I can send more details from my phone.

00:01:06.757 --> 00:01:08.683
The original session on my computer

00:01:08.683 --> 00:01:09.777
continues the work.

00:01:13.217 --> 00:01:15.879
It works the same way for a Xiaohongshu

00:01:15.879 --> 00:01:16.398
draft.

00:01:16.398 --> 00:01:18.930
I can choose a title or ask for a few

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:21.527
paragraphs to be rewritten in the same

00:01:21.527 --> 00:01:22.177
session.

00:01:23.217 --> 00:01:24.077
When it finishes,

00:01:24.077 --> 00:01:25.617
I come back and read the result.

00:01:33.217 --> 00:01:34.975
I have now added phone supervision.

00:01:34.975 --> 00:01:36.591
Once the requirements are clear,

00:01:36.591 --> 00:01:38.586
I can set a goal and let the butler keep

00:01:38.586 --> 00:01:39.537
checking the work.

00:01:40.117 --> 00:01:42.706
This is a controlled demo task.

00:01:42.706 --> 00:01:44.825
I set what it may handle.

00:01:44.825 --> 00:01:47.885
Automatic replies are off by default.

00:01:47.885 --> 00:01:49.298
If I allow them,

00:01:49.298 --> 00:01:52.437
I also set a reply limit and duration.

00:01:53.017 --> 00:01:55.239
The butler checks new records and sends

00:01:55.239 --> 00:01:56.811
messages within that scope.

00:01:56.811 --> 00:01:59.196
It stops when something needs my decision.

00:01:59.196 --> 00:02:00.768
I accept the result myself,

00:02:00.768 --> 00:02:02.937
and I can pause follow-up at any time.

00:02:03.517 --> 00:02:05.299
OpenHands is another option.

00:02:05.299 --> 00:02:07.794
Code still runs on a computer or server.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:10.289
Phone battery restrictions can interrupt

00:02:10.289 --> 00:02:10.824
checks,

00:02:10.824 --> 00:02:12.725
so this part still needs work.

00:02:12.725 --> 00:02:15.161
I want to keep these tasks together and

00:02:15.161 --> 00:02:17.597
spend less time checking every session.
